  "description": "EZIDUP crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C114 H98 Dy4 N6 O24,2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a chain with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.706-3.902 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 106.77-112.97°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C116H106Dy4N6O26.",
